From: Win7 port restore
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: intranet mode switch, online-component hiding, and main-process gates

A single "Intranet Mode" checkbox (Settings → General) turns the app into
an air-gapped posture: everything the app initiates outbound stops, while
user-configured domains (providers, proxies, local paths) are untouched.

Settings & sync:
  - UserSettings.intranetMode + settingsStore.setIntranetMode() with
    optimistic update and rollback; hydrated from GET /api/settings/user.
  - The server broadcasts network_policy_changed on every toggle; chatStore
    mirrors the authoritative value into settingsStore, so every open
    window (and other clients) re-renders immediately — no restart.

UI hiding (first gate, cosmetic only; the main process still enforces):
  - About: update card (check/proxy/release notes) and GitHub/social links.
  - Sidebar: skill-market entry. An already-open market tab shows an
    "unavailable under intranet mode" notice and stops issuing requests.
  - Computer Use: only the "Download Python 3" external-link button hides
    (the offline bundle ships Python); status checks and path config stay.
  - Update store never enters the checking state.

Main-process gates (authoritative, uncached settings read per call):
  - electron/services/intranetMode.ts reads intranetMode from
    <CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR>/settings.json — the same file the server writes;
    the reader lives in the desktop project because the electron bundle
    cannot import server sources.
  - shell.ts openExternalUrl(): http(s) targets are refused before the
    electron module even loads (choke point for IPC + setWindowOpenHandler);
    mailto / system-settings schemes survive.
  - updater.ts checkForUpdates(): returns null without touching
    electron-updater and drops any pending update, so a later download
    has nothing to act on.

Locales: en / zh / zh-TW / jp / kr.

diff --git a/desktop/electron/services/intranetMode.ts b/desktop/electron/services/intranetMode.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4e32a91
--- /dev/null
+++ b/desktop/electron/services/intranetMode.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs'
+import { homedir } from 'node:os'
+import path from 'node:path'
+
+/**
+ * Intranet mode (内网模式) — electron main-process reader.
+ *
+ * The authoritative flag lives in `<CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR>/settings.json`
+ * (default `~/.claude/settings.json`) — the same user-settings file the
+ * server's PUT /api/settings/user writes and the CLI-side
+ * `src/utils/networkPolicy.ts` reads. The main process cannot import that
+ * server source (it lives outside the desktop project), so this tiny reader
+ * mirrors its resolution: config-dir override first, then the home fallback.
+ *
+ * Reads are deliberately UNCACHED: openExternalUrl / checkForUpdates call
+ * this per invocation, so flipping the toggle in any window takes effect in
+ * the main process immediately, without an app restart.
+ */
+
+export function intranetModeSettingsPath(
+  env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env,
+  homeDir: string = homedir(),
+): string {
+  const configDir = env.CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR || path.join(homeDir, '.claude')
+  return path.join(configDir, 'settings.json')
+}
+
+export function isIntranetModeEnabled(
+  env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env,
+  homeDir: string = homedir(),
+): boolean {
+  let raw: string
+  try {
+    raw = readFileSync(intranetModeSettingsPath(env, homeDir), 'utf8')
+  } catch {
+    return false
+  }
+  try {
+    const parsed = JSON.parse(raw) as Record<string, unknown>
+    return parsed?.intranetMode === true
+  } catch {
+    return false
+  }
+}
